# Frontend conventions

Read README.md first. UI profile: <%.UI%>. Keep the same library throughout generated features.

- app/ composes routes, providers and pages. features/<name>/ owns queries, mutations, forms, components and types. Cross-feature imports use public.ts.
- Components/forms use props and callbacks, never transport or query-cache internals. Only feature queries.ts/mutations.ts import api/client.ts. No data-fetching effects.
- Use TanStack Query for server state and TanStack Router for URL state. Keep form/visual state local. Never persist credentials or tenant/auth state in browser storage.
- Go owns permissions, membership, validation and state transitions. UI visibility never grants access. Scope business-query keys by verified actor/session/tenant.
- Auth requests bypass idempotency caching. Cookies remain Secure and HttpOnly; never rewrite cookies or weaken Origin checks. Never put confirmation tokens in URLs.
- Authored files and shared component source are application-owned. catalog.gen.ts and pluto-ui.toml are generator-owned; do not edit them.
- Run npm run fmt and npm run check. Formatter preference is 80 columns; source/generated files stay <=1,000 lines. package-lock.json alone is exempt as machine-owned dependency resolution data. Do not compact code to evade limits.
- Do not scan node_modules, dist, .cert, coverage or binary resources. Retain license notices with copied components.

Theme tokens and mode live in pluto.toml. Never edit src/generated/theme*.css or
public/pluto-theme.js; run npm run theme:generate. Custom selectors belong in the
configured application-owned overrides CSS. Preserve the import precedence and
external prepaint bootstrap. Never bundle the TOML document into browser code.


Use npm run fmt, not plain Prettier, as the final TS/TSX formatting command.
The visible scripts/readability.mjs policy requires expanded control blocks,
braces, separated object/type members and logical blank lines. Avoid nested
ternaries. npm run lint checks canonical formatting without writes; formatter
regression tests run with npm test. Split files before hitting the 1,000-line limit.


Across languages, separate standalone comment blocks from the preceding line with
one blank line, except at line 1. Keep comment groups and next-line directives
attached to their following code; preserve trailing inline comments.

Every asynchronous action must acknowledge immediately with accessible pending
feedback and a clear outcome. Use the published action helpers; keep transport
in feature mutations. Choose optimism explicitly for predictable operations,
project over current scoped data and reconcile with server truth. Preserve input
on errors, block conflicting writes, fence scope changes, and treat timeout as
uncertain rather than rejection. Keep stable backend idempotency keys separate.
Test held responses, rejection, uncertain outcomes and concurrent/scope changes.
